invariant: INV-74
file: src/tcp_seal.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_seal_in_place takes a side buffer shorter than one KeyUpdate
  record, so the KeyUpdate an owed answer writes, or the alert of a
  failure, has no room and the seal of it refuses after the call started.
  The loop requires CH_EINVAL with nothing written for a side one byte
  short.

--- old
    if (result == NULL || side == NULL || side_cap < CH_KEY_UPDATE_RECORD_LEN ||
--- new
    if (result == NULL || side == NULL || side_cap == 0 ||
